      "role": "user",
      "content": "i see what you mean. it really highlights how the senator's approach is just more realistic for the real world. do you think it's possible to actually write a character like the activist who has a coherent, logical counter-argument that actually challenges the senator's math, or are they just fundamentally incapable of seeing things realistically because they're so driven by emotion?",
